    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nPerhaps not really a bug, but a very trivially reproducible example so I felt like it might be worth to report it anyways. (please feel free to close if that's just expected behaviour and a false positive example, thanks)\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nDefault settings of `mini.ai` (matching those in lazyvim).\r\n\r\nBuffer text is (note the evil `'` in the comment... that's what seemingly messes it up).\r\n```\r\n-- user's options\r\nlocal opts = {\r\n  a = 'a',\r\n  b = 'b',\r\n}\r\n```\r\nwith the cursor on word `local`.\r\n\r\nType `vinq`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`'a'` is selected.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n<img width=\"168\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/2418513/4a56d228-0912-4c51-928b-40d1cbe062ad\">",
