            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for taking your time opening this!\r\n\r\nYes, this is not really a bug. 'mini.ai' first looks within current line for the textobject and then within multiple lines neighborhood if it doesn't find one. In this case it is already inside multiline `iq` textobject, so it tries to look for the next, which is the one in your screenshot. If you try the same with cursor on `a = `, you'll get `'a'` selected as it is on the same line.",
